Subject: [PATCH] feat(invoices): manual status control + accrual on draft exit
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two gaps this closes:

1. update_invoice_status_v1 was written assuming draft->sent/viewed/
   partial/overdue is a pure status write with 'no ledger impact.'
   create_invoice_v1 (prior commit) made that false: an invoice
   created as draft (the form default) and later sent — either via
   'Send to Client', which calls this same RPC, or a manual status
   change — never got its debit-AR/credit-revenue accrual posted at
   all. Same underlying bug as before, just reachable through a
   different path. Fixed by posting the entry the first time an
   invoice leaves draft, guarded against double-posting by checking
   for an existing entry with the invoice's reference.

2. There was no manual way to move an invoice through draft -> sent
   -> viewed -> partial -> overdue by hand — only automatic (email
   send) and the two accounting actions (Mark Paid / Void) existed.
   Added a 'Set status' section to InvoiceActions' dropdown wired to
   the existing (now-fixed) useUpdateInvoiceStatus hook, disabled once
   an invoice is paid or voided since those have their own dedicated,
   accounting-aware actions.
